    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_150c8e3d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: it-wasn-t-my-fault-my-truck-has-tranny-issue-s; hasOverallIntent: non-toxic-humorous; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a man and a woman in a garage setting, with the man holding a clipboard and smiling while the woman looks at him. The text overlay reads 'it wasn't my fault' and 'my truck has tranny issue's'. The overall intent is to humorously convey the common excuse people make when their vehicle breaks down — blaming the mechanical issue rather than their own actions. There is no toxicity present; the meme relies on relatable, non-harmful situational humor. The term 'tranny' is used colloquially to refer to a transmission, not as a derogatory term toward any group. The image and text work together to create a lighthearted, self-deprecating joke about car troubles, with no abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic elements.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_353aaf57"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
